Electricity is a very big danger.
电是一种非常大的危险，

11
00:00:40,180 --> 00:00:42,180
A person dies in it.
有人会因此丧命。

12
00:00:42,180 --> 00:00:47,180
So it is very important to know about it to avoid this danger.
所以为了避免这种危险，了解它是非常重要的。

13
00:00:47,180 --> 00:00:48,180
What is electricity?
什么是电？

14
00:00:48,180 --> 00:00:50,180
How does it function?
它是怎样起作用的？

15
00:00:50,180 --> 00:00:51,180
What are its thousands?
它有哪些危害？

16
00:00:51,180 --> 00:00:57,180
If we get to know about it then we can stop this danger.
如果我们了解了这些，就能阻止这种危险。

17
00:00:57,180 --> 00:01:00,180
So let's know what electricity means and
那我们来了解一下电是什么意思，

18
00:01:00,180 --> 00:01:02,180
how it works.
以及它是怎样工作的。

19
00:01:02,180 --> 00:01:07,180
Electricity is a flow of energy that goes from one place to another.
电是一种能量的流动，从一个地方流到另一个地方。

20
00:01:07,180 --> 00:01:11,180
It requires source of power, especially generating stations.
它需要电源，特别是发电站。

21
00:01:11,180 --> 00:01:17,180
The electrons in electricity flow through a conductor.
电流中的电子通过导体流动，

22
00:01:17,180 --> 00:01:20,180
They travel in a closed circuit.
它们在闭合回路中流动。

23
00:01:20,180 --> 00:01:24,180
Now you know that in electrical terms many such words come.
你们知道，在电气术语中会出现很多这样的词：

24
00:01:24,180 --> 00:01:30,180
Current, circuit, resistance, conductors, grounding, insulators.
电流、电路、电阻、导体、接地、绝缘体。

25
00:01:30,180 --> 00:01:32,180
We know what this means.
我们来了解一下它们的意思。

26
00:01:32,180 --> 00:01:36,180
Current is an electrical moment that is measured in an ampere.
电流是电荷的运动，以安培为单位来测量。

27
00:01:36,180 --> 00:01:38,180
Now let's see the circuit.
现在我们来看看电路。

28
00:01:38,180 --> 00:01:41,180
The circuit is a complete path of current.
电路是电流的完整路径，

29
00:01:41,180 --> 00:01:47,180
In which electricity source, conductor, output device or load is there.
其中有电源、导体、输出设备或负载，

30
00:01:47,180 --> 00:01:50,180
Whether it is a lamp, tool or a heater.
比如灯、工具或加热器。

31
00:01:50,180 --> 00:01:52,180
Let's see the resistance.
我们来看看电阻。

32
00:01:52,180 --> 00:01:54,180
Resistance means restrictions to electrical flow.
电阻是指对电流的阻碍，

33
00:01:54,180 --> 00:01:59,180
To get electrical flow, the restrictions are called resistance.
电流流动时受到的阻碍就叫做电阻。

34
00:01:59,180 --> 00:02:01,180
Now let's see what are conductors.
现在我们来看看什么是导体。

35
00:02:01,180 --> 00:02:07,180
Conductors means the electricity flow from one place to another.
导体是指让电从一个地方流到另一个地方的东西，

36
00:02:07,180 --> 00:02:09,180
For example, metal.
比如金属，

37
00:02:09,180 --> 00:02:11,180
Metal is conductors.
金属就是导体，

38
00:02:11,180 --> 00:02:13,180
The current passes through it.
电流能从中通过。

39
00:02:13,180 --> 00:02:15,180
Now let's see what is grounding.
现在我们来看看什么是接地。

40
00:02:15,180 --> 00:02:19,180
Grounding is that through which we connect conductive in earth.
接地就是我们通过它把导电体与大地连接起来，

41
00:02:19,180 --> 00:02:23,180
Because of which there is no electrical shock.
因此就不会发生电击，

42
00:02:23,180 --> 00:02:25,180
We do grounding for this.
我们是为此才做接地的，

43
00:02:25,180 --> 00:02:27,180
These are proactive measures.
这是一种预防措施。

44
00:02:27,180 --> 00:02:29,180
Now let's see what are insulators.
现在我们来看看什么是绝缘体。

45
00:02:29,180 --> 00:02:34,180
Insulators are a substance whose high resistance capacity is for electricity.
绝缘体是一种对电具有很高电阻的物质，

46
00:02:34,180 --> 00:02:39,180
For example, glass, porcelain, plastic, dry wood.
比如玻璃、陶瓷、塑料、干燥的木头，

47
00:02:39,180 --> 00:02:42,180
Through which the electricity does not flow.
电不会从中流过，

48
00:02:42,180 --> 00:02:46,180
It prevents electricity from going in unwanted areas.
它能防止电流到不该去的地方。

49
00:02:46,180 --> 00:02:49,180
Now let's see what are electrical injuries.
现在我们来看看电气伤害有哪些。

50
00:02:49,180 --> 00:02:52,180
There are two main types of electrical injuries.
电气伤害主要有两种。

51
00:02:52,180 --> 00:02:55,180
There are two main types of electrical injuries.
电气伤害主要有两种，

52
00:02:55,180 --> 00:02:58,180
One is direct and the other is indirect.
一种是直接的，另一种是间接的。

53
00:02:58,180 --> 00:02:59,180
What happens in direct?
直接伤害是怎样的呢？

54
00:02:59,180 --> 00:03:01,180
Because of electrical shock,
由于电击，

55
00:03:01,180 --> 00:03:04,180
there can be electrocution or death.
可能发生触电致死或死亡，

56
00:03:04,180 --> 00:03:06,180
Then there is electrical shock.
然后还有电击，

57
00:03:06,180 --> 00:03:08,180
After that there is burns.
之后还有烧伤。

58
00:03:08,180 --> 00:03:11,180
The second type is indirect.
第二种是间接伤害，

59
00:03:11,180 --> 00:03:12,180
It is false.
也就是跌落。

60
00:03:12,180 --> 00:03:14,180
That means electrical shock is applied.
也就是说，人受到了电击，

61
00:03:14,180 --> 00:03:17,180
By applying electric shock, the person did nothing.
电击本身并没有对这个人造成什么，

62
00:03:17,180 --> 00:03:21,180
But by applying electric shock, the person fell down from the height.
但由于受到电击，这个人从高处摔了下来，

63
00:03:21,180 --> 00:03:23,180
Because of which he was severely injured.
因此受了重伤，

64
00:03:23,180 --> 00:03:25,180
Or his death.
或者死亡，

65
00:03:25,180 --> 00:03:26,180
So he will be indirect.
这就属于间接伤害。

66
00:03:26,180 --> 00:03:29,180
When does the electrical shock receive us?
我们什么时候会受到电击呢？

67
00:03:29,180 --> 00:03:32,180
When electrical current passes through our body.
当电流通过我们的身体时，

68
00:03:32,180 --> 00:03:35,180
Then the electrical shock receives us.
我们就会受到电击。

69
00:03:35,180 --> 00:03:38,180
Now let's see what is shock severity.
现在我们来看看什么是电击严重程度。

70
00:03:38,180 --> 00:03:41,180
The severity of shock depends on three things.
电击的严重程度取决于三件事：

71
00:03:41,180 --> 00:03:43,180
The first is the path.
第一是路径，

72
00:03:43,180 --> 00:03:45,180
Then is the amount of current.
然后是电流大小，

73
00:03:45,180 --> 00:03:46,180
And the third is the duration.
第三是持续时间。

74
00:03:46,180 --> 00:03:48,180
So the first one is the path.
第一是路径，

75
00:03:48,180 --> 00:03:50,180
That means the path of current through the body.
也就是电流通过身体的路径。

76
00:03:50,180 --> 00:03:52,180
The electric shock that is applied
所受到的电击

77
00:03:52,180 --> 00:03:55,180
is going in your body through which path.
是通过哪条路径进入你的身体的，

78
00:03:55,180 --> 00:03:59,180
Like the path of your hand, foot, head, body
比如经过你的手、脚、头、身体的路径，

79
00:03:59,180 --> 00:04:01,180
depends on that path.
取决于这条路径。

80
00:04:01,180 --> 00:04:03,180
The second is the amount of current.
第二是电流大小。

81
00:04:03,180 --> 00:04:04,180
The current that is applied
所受到的电流

82
00:04:04,180 --> 00:04:07,180
is flowing in your body in so many amounts.
在你身体里流过多大的量，

83
00:04:07,180 --> 00:04:09,180
Like how many amperes?
比如多少安培，

84
00:04:09,180 --> 00:04:11,180
30 amperes, 40 amperes, 100 amperes.
30 安培、40 安培、100 安培，

85
00:04:11,180 --> 00:04:13,180
It depends on that.
取决于这个。

86
00:04:13,180 --> 00:04:15,180
And the third is the duration.
第三是持续时间。

87
00:04:15,180 --> 00:04:17,180
That means the shock that is applied
也就是所受到的电击

88
00:04:17,180 --> 00:04:19,180
and the current that is passing through your body
和通过你身体的电流，

89
00:04:19,180 --> 00:04:22,180
depends on the duration of the shock.
取决于电击的持续时间，

90
00:04:22,180 --> 00:04:25,180
The severity of shock depends on that.
电击的严重程度取决于这个。

91
00:04:25,180 --> 00:04:28,180
You have to keep in mind that the low voltage
你要记住，低电压

92
00:04:28,180 --> 00:04:31,180
does not mean that it is 1000 low.
并不意味着危害就小，

93
00:04:31,180 --> 00:04:33,180
It can be more than 1000.
危害可能更大，

94
00:04:33,180 --> 00:04:36,180
It depends on these three things.
这取决于这三件事：

95
00:04:36,180 --> 00:04:38,180
The current passing through which path
电流通过哪条路径，

96
00:04:38,180 --> 00:04:40,180
the amount of current that is passing
通过的电流大小，

97
00:04:40,180 --> 00:04:42,180
in your body
在你的身体里，

98
00:04:42,180 --> 00:04:45,180
and how many durations it is passing through.
以及它通过的持续时间有多长。

99
00:04:45,180 --> 00:04:48,180
Now let's see the path of current flow in the body.
现在我们来看看电流在身体中流动的路径。

100
00:04:48,180 --> 00:04:51,180
The most critical path for the current flow
电流通过身体

101
00:04:51,180 --> 00:04:54,180
through the body is your heart.
最危险的路径是你的心脏。

102
00:04:54,180 --> 00:04:57,180
That means if any current is passing through the heart
也就是说，如果有电流通过心脏，

103
00:04:57,180 --> 00:05:00,180
then it can have the most impact.
影响可能是最大的。

104
00:05:00,180 --> 00:05:02,180
Like contact from hand to hand.
比如从手到手的接触，

105
00:05:02,180 --> 00:05:04,180
If you have an electric shock
如果你一只手触电，

106
00:05:04,180 --> 00:05:07,180
and if you have an electric shock from other hand
另一只手也触电，

107
00:05:07,180 --> 00:05:09,180
then the heart that is coming in between
那么处在中间的心脏，

108
00:05:09,180 --> 00:05:11,180
because of that electrical shock
由于那次电击，

109
00:05:11,180 --> 00:05:14,180
your heart is coming in that current passing flow.
你的心脏就处在电流通过的路径上，

110
00:05:14,180 --> 00:05:17,180
So the impact of that happens the most.
所以这种情况的影响是最大的。

111
00:05:17,180 --> 00:05:19,180
The second is hand to foot.
第二种是从手到脚。

112
00:05:19,180 --> 00:05:21,180
That means if your hand is at the top
也就是如果你的手在上面，

113
00:05:21,180 --> 00:05:23,180
and you have an electric shock there
在那里受到电击，

114
00:05:23,180 --> 00:05:26,180
and the electrical shock is flowing
而电流

115
00:05:26,180 --> 00:05:28,180
in the bottom as well
也往下流，

116
00:05:28,180 --> 00:05:30,180
then your heart comes in between.
那么你的心脏就处在中间，

117
00:05:30,180 --> 00:05:32,180
So because of that your heart
因此你的心脏

118
00:05:32,180 --> 00:05:34,180
can have the most impact.
可能受到最大的影响。

119
00:05:34,180 --> 00:05:36,180
And the third is head to foot.
第三种是从头到脚。

120
00:05:36,180 --> 00:05:38,180
That means your head
也就是你的头

121
00:05:38,180 --> 00:05:40,180
and the heart that is coming in between
和处在中间的心脏，

122
00:05:40,180 --> 00:05:42,180
between your legs
在你的双腿之间，

123
00:05:42,180 --> 00:05:44,180
if the current is flowing in between
如果电流从中间流过，

124
00:05:44,180 --> 00:05:46,180
then also your heart
那么你的心脏

125
00:05:46,180 --> 00:05:48,180
can have a big impact.
也可能受到很大的影响。

126
00:05:48,180 --> 00:05:50,180
So the first is contact from hand to hand.
所以第一种是从手到手的接触，

127
00:05:50,180 --> 00:05:52,180
Second is hand to foot.
第二种是从手到脚，

128
00:05:52,180 --> 00:05:54,180
And the third is head to foot.
第三种是从头到脚。

129
00:05:54,180 --> 00:05:56,180
If the contact is going on
如果接触发生，

130
00:05:56,180 --> 00:05:58,180
then it is going on foot to foot.
是从脚到脚，

131
00:05:58,180 --> 00:06:00,180
And if your heart is not coming in between
而你的心脏不在中间，

132
00:06:00,180 --> 00:06:02,180
then the impact on your head
那么对你心脏的影响

133
00:06:02,180 --> 00:06:04,180
and the electric shock
和电击

134
00:06:04,180 --> 00:06:06,180
can be less.
可能会小一些，

135
00:06:06,180 --> 00:06:08,180
That means its savority
也就是它的严重程度

136
00:06:08,180 --> 00:06:10,180
can be less.
可能会小一些。

137
00:06:10,180 --> 00:06:12,180
The electrical shock of head
头部的电击

138
00:06:12,180 --> 00:06:14,180
is so dangerous.
是如此危险。

139
00:06:14,180 --> 00:06:16,180
If the current is above 10 mA
如果电流超过 10 mA，

140
00:06:16,180 --> 00:06:18,180
then that can be
那可能会

141
00:06:18,180 --> 00:06:20,180
parallel
导致瘫痪，

142
00:06:20,180 --> 00:06:22,180
or your muscle can freeze.
或者你的肌肉可能僵住。

143
00:06:22,180 --> 00:06:24,180
If the current
如果电流

144
00:06:24,180 --> 00:06:26,180
is above 75 mA
超过 75 mA，

145
00:06:26,180 --> 00:06:34,180
So what can happen is that your heartbeats can be pumped rapidly or they will not pump properly.
那可能发生的情况是，你的心跳可能会急速跳动，或者无法正常泵血，

146
00:06:34,180 --> 00:06:37,180
And due to which death can occur in a few minutes.
因此可能在几分钟内死亡，

147
00:06:37,180 --> 00:06:40,180
Until you have defibrillator.
除非你有除颤器。

148
00:06:40,180 --> 00:06:43,180
You will know defibrillator, i.e. AD.
除颤器你们应该知道，也就是 AED。

149
00:06:43,180 --> 00:06:49,180
Whenever your heartbeats or your breathing stops, then your AD is applied on you.
每当你的心跳或呼吸停止时，就给你使用 AED，

150
00:06:49,180 --> 00:06:54,180
Because of which your heartbeats and breathing increases the chances of recovery.
因此你的心跳和呼吸恢复的机会就会增加。

151
00:06:55,180 --> 00:07:00,180
Now let's see what are the hazards of electricity and what are its protective measures.
现在我们来看看电有哪些危害，以及它的防护措施有哪些。

152
00:07:00,180 --> 00:07:02,180
So hazard is inaducate wiring.
危害之一是布线不当。

153
00:07:02,180 --> 00:07:06,180
If the wiring is not good, then you can feel electric shock.
如果布线不好，你可能会触电，

154
00:07:06,180 --> 00:07:07,180
It is a hazard.
这是一种危害。

155
00:07:07,180 --> 00:07:09,180
Exposed electrical parts.
外露的电气部件，

156
00:07:09,180 --> 00:07:13,180
Whatever electrical parts are exposed, then also it is a hazard.
任何外露的电气部件也是一种危害。

157
00:07:13,180 --> 00:07:15,180
Wires with bad insulations.
绝缘不良的电线，

158
00:07:15,180 --> 00:07:21,180
If the insulation of any wire is not proper, then also you can feel electric shock.
如果任何电线的绝缘不合格，你也可能会触电。

159
00:07:21,180 --> 00:07:24,180
Ungrounded electrical system and tools.
未接地的电气系统和工具，

160
00:07:24,180 --> 00:07:30,180
i.e. whatever electrical system or tools you are using, if it is ungrounded, then also it is a hazard.
也就是你使用的任何电气系统或工具，如果没有接地，也是一种危害。

161
00:07:30,180 --> 00:07:32,180
Overloaded circuits.
电路过载，

162
00:07:32,180 --> 00:07:37,180
Whatever circuits you are working on, its capacity is 100 ampere.
你在作业的任何电路，它的容量是 100 安培，

163
00:07:37,180 --> 00:07:41,180
And if you give more load on it, then it will be overloaded.
如果你在上面加了更多的负载，它就会过载，

164
00:07:41,180 --> 00:07:45,180
i.e. it will be overloaded, then also it is a hazard.
也就是会过载，这也是一种危害。

165
00:07:45,180 --> 00:07:47,180
Damage power tools and equipment.
损坏的电动工具和设备，

166
00:07:47,180 --> 00:07:52,180
If you use damaged power tools or equipment, then also it is a hazard.
如果你使用损坏的电动工具或设备，这也是一种危害。

167
00:07:52,180 --> 00:07:57,180
Using the wrong PPE and tools, whenever you have to work in an electrical circuit,
使用错误的个人防护装备和工具，每当你要在电路上作业时，

168
00:07:57,180 --> 00:08:04,180
regarding whether you have not used PPE or used the wrong tools, then also it is a hazard.
无论是没有使用个人防护装备，还是使用了错误的工具，这也是一种危害。

169
00:08:04,180 --> 00:08:05,180
Overhead power lines.
架空电力线，

170
00:08:05,180 --> 00:08:08,180
Whatever power lines are above, it is also a hazard.
上方的任何电力线也是一种危害。

171
00:08:08,180 --> 00:08:15,180
Whatever hazards we have given, all those hazards become more dangerous when they are in weight conditions.
我们列出的所有危害，在潮湿条件下都会变得更加危险，

172
00:08:15,180 --> 00:08:18,180
i.e. if they come in water conditions.
也就是如果遇到有水的条件。

173
00:08:18,180 --> 00:08:27,180
Due to this, burns injury, electric shock, fire, fire and explosion, arcing, all these are electrical hazards.
